<h4>What changed</h4>
<p>K3.1 Pro is not a new model but <strong>K3 trained further</strong>. Its size (2.8 trillion total, 104 billion active) and 1-million-token context are unchanged. Moonshot credits the gains to a much larger post-training compute budget. It ran <strong>reinforcement learning</strong> (training that shapes a model by rewarding good behavior) across hundreds of task domains at once, rather than fine-tuning separately for each, it says.</p>
