<p>The price cut stands out. K3 was called &ldquo;Opus-class at Sonnet prices,&rdquo; and K3.1 Pro takes another third off that. The weights ship in a 4-bit format (MXFP4), about 1.56 TB to download, and estimates say running them yourself takes a server on the order of eight B300 GPUs. The model card lists vLLM, SGLang and TokenSpeed as recommended inference engines.</p>

<h4>Scores: one step behind Opus 5.5</h4>
<p>The number Moonshot led with is a terminal-task test. By its own figures it is 0.7 points behind Claude Opus 5.5.</p>
